WEBVTT

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.570
Oh? You're over an hour early today.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.250
Oh, well, break's over, and I'm free today,

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.570
so I was hoping someone 
could play against me.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.330
Play against? Like a rally? 
Someone to feed you the ball?

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.750
Oh, I meant a match.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.670
You want a match?

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.220
You just played in the finals two days ago.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.480
I was thinking of ways to 
change the pace in a game,

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.100
and I came up with a few 
tactics I think I can use.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.780
As tired as I was after losing the final,

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.250
I'd still rather play again than rest.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.180
Looks like you're addicted 
to playing matches.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:43.930
Huh?

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.690
Addicted?

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.040
An intense battle like that 
final match two days ago

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.040
is both frightening and stressful,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.700
but it's also a thrill you 
can't experience elsewhere.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.000
Oh...

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.760
Regardless, I understand how you feel.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.030
I am a former pro, after all.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.680
Can't help it if no one else is here.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.210
I'll play you.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.160
You, Aoi-san?

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.210
What, is that a problem?

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.050
Not at all. Is your injury okay?

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.490
I can handle one set.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.190
Go warm up already.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:19.460
O-Okay!

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.070
Gathering of Rivals

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.330
All right, I won!

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:05.800
<i>Damn it...</i>

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.580
<i>He's a former pro, all right.</i>

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.980
Guess I've still got it, 
so long as it's a one-set match.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.580
Thank you very much.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.650
Oh, Bro! You're here early.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:16.590
Yukichi-kun!

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:22.800
<i>He doesn't have a lot of tournament 
experience in the first place.</i>

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:24.970
<i>You practice changing the pace</i>

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:28.810
<i>by getting the opportunity 
to hit different shots.</i>

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.370
<i>He needs to learn how to deal 
with left-handed play, too.</i>

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.240
<i>I'll have to help him out.</i>

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:44.880
<i>If I don't win the All-Japan Junior, 
I'll have to give up on going pro.</i>

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.560
<i>Can I really quit trying to go pro?</i>

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:00.000
So you're in Class 2, Ei-chan?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.630
And you're in Class 4.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.720
I'm in Class 3.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.500
Looks like we're all split up this year.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.900
And you're in Class 6, the science class.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.320
What's wrong, Ei-chan?

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.460
Are you sad that we're 
all in separate classes?

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:13.730
That hurts, Kageyama.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.640
Don't worry!

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.570
I'll still come to your 
matches to cheer you on.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.730
Me, too!

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.990
I'll cheer you on, too...

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.490
Maruo-kun.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.660
Okay, thanks.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.160
Congratulations on advancing to the next grade.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.740
Today, you begin your third year of high school.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:34.880
A year from now, you'll all 
be walking your own paths.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.250
I'd like you all to keep that in mind

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.280
as you consider how you'll spend this year.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:46.480
I had to enroll in the cram 
school by the train station.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.760
Guess I'll have to start buckling 
down after club's over.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.050
<i>Everyone's starting to switch in exam mode.</i>

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.640
Man, you're way behind.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.430
I have to go to an open campus 
tour over spring break, too.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.900
<i>I sort of feel like I'm fighting 
the current with all my might.</i>

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.460
Ei-chan, ready to go?

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.530
Yeah.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:08.610
Everyone's suddenly talking about 
entrance exams now that we're third-years.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.410
It sort of feels like we're being alienated.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.860
Yeah...

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.300
It was like this during the field trip too, but...

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.670
Hey, are you listening, Ei-chan?

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.240
What? Yeah!

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.360
I'm listening.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.590
My class is in exam mode, too.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.600
Yeah... I thought so.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:36.440
<i>If I have to give up on going pro...</i>

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:40.370
<i>Could I still stay by Nat-chan's side?</i>

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.930
I caught it, I caught it!

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:47.910
I'm not surprised. You have 
great hand-eye coordination.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.240
All right, gather 'round.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.370
Starting today, we're going 
to train a little differently.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.770
Oh?

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:57.620
We're going to go practical,

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.260
so you should all have 
individual goals in mind.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:01.550
<i>Practical?</i>

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.130
Hey!

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.750
Oh, they're here.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.130
Thanks for having us!

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:10.030
A-Araya-kun!

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:11.140
Hey.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:13.550
And Miyagawa-kun and Mogami-kun!

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:14.220
Hi.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.480
Huh? Even Iwasa-kun?

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:18.900
What? Why?

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:22.440
There was a meeting of Kanagawa
tennis clubs the other day.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.940
It was decided that, starting this year, 
players would train more

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.950
with other clubs to help 
strengthen junior players.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:33.560
If you do well at the Kanto 
tournament or the nationals,

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:36.380
you'll earn more opportunities 
to compete in Kanagawa.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.090
Then what about Iwasa-kun?

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:39.960
He isn't a junior player, is he?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.930
I invited him.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:46.730
I'm here because they agreed to allow 
me to sketch during my free time.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.980
I didn't get into art school, 
so I have lots of time on my hands.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:56.270
I really think he can give you some 
good hints about changing the pace.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:07:00.980
Of course, STC will be sending 
players to other clubs, as well.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.230
<i>This is awesome.</i>

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:04.810
<i>If we do this often,</i>

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.470
<i>I'll get to play a lot of matches!</i>

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:12.030
And there should be one more girl coming...

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.620
I'm sorry we're late.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:19.700
A... girl?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.520
Thank you for coming all this way.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:25.630
Not at all. Thank you for inviting us.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.760
We were planning a trip to Tokyo anyway,

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.290
so the timing is perfect.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.040
Come on, introduce yourself, too.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:35.600
My hair's stuck...

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:40.050
Aki-chan!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.270
<i>It's Nat-chan's rival, Shimizu-san.</i>

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.900
<i>Isn't she the top-ranked 
player in the girls' division?</i>

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:52.200
We have about three months 
left until the Kanto Junior.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.190
Starting today, Kanagawa will 
treat these three months

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:58.660
as an enhanced training period
with regular inter-club practices.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:04.660
Only players who have achieved results 
of a certain level are here today.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.550
After basic training, 
you'll be playing matches,

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.920
so when your name is called, 
head to the designated court.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.430
<i>This is my chance to get some match experience!</i>

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:20.640
Hey, Araya-kun!

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.940
You're yelling too loud. 
No one can concentrate!

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:26.120
There are plenty of people who yell out loud!

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:28.610
I'm saying you're <i>too</i> loud, Araya-kun!

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.610
You won't get any stronger if you 
can't ignore the little things!

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.640
You won't get any girls that way!

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:36.490
What?!

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.950
Hey, you two! Take this seriously!

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:44.110
Maybe there's something neither of 
them will yield, as fellow baseliners.

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.430
But their rallies are really high-level.

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:48.960
Well, Maruo-kun, want to start?

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.090
Whenever you're ready!

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:56.090
<i>Iwasa-kun can hit any shot at any speed,</i>

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:58.680
<i>along any course, at any timing.</i>

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:03.770
<i>That's a skill I'll need in order to be 
able to change the pace of a match.</i>

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.310
<i>First, a flat power shot!</i>

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:11.130
<i>Impressive!</i>

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:14.190
<i>It should be easier to return 
a fast ball with a fast ball,</i>

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:16.670
<i>but he easily slowed the pace and went deep.</i>

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:18.450
<i>How about a low slice, then?</i>

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:22.950
<i>He keeps changing the pace 
without breaking a sweat!</i>

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:26.030
<i>All right, I should start by watching him.</i>

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:29.380
<i>How does Iwasa-kun change the pace so easily?</i>

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:32.580
<i>What does he do differently 
from me and everyone else?</i>

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:35.340
<i>What's the most effective 
way to change the pace?</i>

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:39.220
Um, Iwasa-kun!

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:43.620
Is there a trick to returning fast shots slowly?

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:44.790
Er, what?

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:48.510
Returning fast shots... slowly?

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:49.350
Yeah!

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:51.320
Grab it, then throw it...

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.360
I guess.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:54.850
Grab it...

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.170
then throw it?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.230
What?

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:02.370
Um, it'd be great if you
could be more specific.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.870
Huh? I thought I was being 
pretty specific just now.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:10.070
<i>Oh! He plays intuitively, 
just like Nat-chan.</i>

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:13.040
Maruo, you're facing Araya next.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.800
O-Okay.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.170
<i>I guess I just have to figure it out myself.</i>

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:23.540
<i>Araya-kun is the top 
left-handed player in the nation.</i>

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:27.020
<i>He's the best training partner to 
get me used to left-handed players.</i>

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:30.940
<i>I don't know what kinds of 
players I'll face from here on.</i>

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:33.940
<i>No matter who I face, I want 
to be able to control the ball</i>

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.580
<i>and change the pace to 
whatever I want it to be.</i>

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.240
Amazing...

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.760
The list of things I need to do

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:42.940
in the next three months just keeps growing.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.670
Aki-chan, what's wrong?

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.100
You were spacing out.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:58.380
Oh, nothing...

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:02.510
I just thought it was impressive, 
taking notes and stuff.

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:04.190
Oh, you mean Ei-chan?

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:06.550
He really is impressive.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:08.180
Ei-chan-san...

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.430
He's really into tennis.

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:13.950
He only started playing two years ago, 
but he just keeps getting better.

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:19.040
Ei-chan-san seems to be having a lot of fun.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:27.250
So anyway, what's it like having 
your mom as your coach?

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:30.210
Huh? What it's like?

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.150
It's been that way for as long 
as I can remember, so...

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:36.710
Yeah? Now that you mention it, I've been 
at STC as long as I can remember, too.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.320
I'm sorry I wasn't any help.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.000
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.220
I get that there's nothing 
you can compare it to.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.610
Ready to have them switch us in?

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:47.220
Oh, sure.

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:56.180
Thank you for including Aki in this today.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:58.060
The pleasure is all ours.

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:01.950
Having Japan's best player come 
in is more than we could ask for.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.960
The truth is, for a long time,

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:08.200
I've wanted an opportunity to observe 
Takasaki Natsu-san's training environment.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:09.740
Natsu's?

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:11.420
Why is that?

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:16.120
I believe the only player capable of 
defeating Aki at the All-Japan Junior

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.210
this year is Natsu-san.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.720
The difference in ability between 
them is smaller every year.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:26.720
And yet Aki herself doesn't seem 
to be worried about it at all.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:31.730
So I thought it might spark something 
in her if she saw how her rival trained.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.470
I see.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.850
But why isn't she worried, I wonder?

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:39.450
She's been training solely 
with me since she was young,

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:43.350
so I think she lacks a competitive 
spirit toward players her own age.

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:46.590
I've spoken to her about this before, but...

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:50.080
Perhaps she's just at that age.

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:53.210
I don't know if it's because she's 
starting to think for herself now,

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.940
but she takes her time on 
every little thing she does.

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:57.760
It's quite frustrating to watch.

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:09.850
Ah, what a nice breeze!

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:13.620
Hello.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.190
Oh, hello.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:20.860
Um, do you remember me?

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.480
Yeah, we met at the indoor invitational.

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:24.610
Shimizu-san, right?

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:27.610
You dropped your cell phone 
battery near the courts.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:28.810
That's right.

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:31.620
Yesterday, my mother told 
me we'd be going to STC,

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:34.850
and I was wondering whether 
I'd run into you again.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:37.070
I'm surprised that I did!

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:38.880
I was surprised, too!

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:42.630
This will be the second time.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:44.210
That's right.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.970
Well, good luck with your practice matches.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:52.640
W-Wait a second, please!

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.510
Um... I mean...

00:13:57.090 --> 00:14:00.150
You really... love tennis, don't you?

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:00.900
Huh?

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:04.150
Well, yeah, I do.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:07.290
Oh... I'm sorry.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:09.830
That must be true of everyone here, right?

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:11.280
Wh-What?

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.580
I saw you playing earlier,

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:17.290
and you looked like you were 
having so much fun, so I just...

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.970
Huh? Oh, did I?

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:22.540
But you love it too, don't you, Shimizu-san?

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:26.420
When you're that good,
it must be really fun.

00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:31.600
I'm actually not really sure.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:34.810
Oh, it's not that I hate it.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:39.180
But by the time I realized it, 
my mother was already my coach,

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:41.610
and being on the court was 
a part of my everyday life.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:46.170
Tennis is all I've ever done.

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:52.430
Aki! It's almost time.

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:53.190
Oh...

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:54.920
See you later.

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:57.910
Here!

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:05.960
<i>Does that mean Shimizu-san's been playing 
tennis constantly since she was little?</i>

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.940
<i>If that's been her everyday life, 
it's no wonder she's so good.</i>

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:13.640
Okay, let's start the matches on each court.

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:26.190
<i>I wonder if I said something strange earlier.</i>

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:29.640
<i>Tennis always took priority for me,</i>

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:33.470
<i>and there were times I didn't like having 
a different lifestyle from everyone else.</i>

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:38.590
<i>But because I was always 
guided in the right direction,</i>

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:41.710
<i>in the end, I thought I was 
happier than everyone else.</i>

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:44.970
<i>But I wonder what it is...</i>

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:47.960
<i>Something is different.</i>

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:57.220
<i>Is this really what's fun for me?</i>

00:15:58.090 --> 00:15:59.220
Yeah!

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:02.230
Damn. I lost, huh?

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:05.230
All right, that's it for today!

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:07.830
I want to train at your club one day, too!

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:08.800
Yeah, definitely!

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:11.680
Thank you very much for today.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:14.240
Not at all. I hope we 
were of help to you, too.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.940
Bye, Bro. I'm heading out.

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:16.950
See you tomorrow.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:20.020
Um... Maruo-kun?

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:21.960
Oh, Shimizu-san.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:23.970
Um...

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:26.420
Aki! Let's go.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:30.470
Th-Thank you for today!

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:32.720
Oh, uh, sure...

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:35.940
<i>It seemed like she wanted to say something.</i>

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:42.680
Today was such a surprise.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.900
But it was a great experience.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:45.920
Yeah.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:49.110
What?

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:51.690
You beat Shimizu-san today?

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:55.120
But Aki-chan wasn't in top form today.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:58.580
Maybe she's working through 
things by trial and error.

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:01.200
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.580
You really... love tennis, don't you?

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:08.370
Hey.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:11.590
You love tennis, right, Nat-chan?

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:14.590
Of course I do.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:17.420
I knew you'd say that.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:21.100
How about you, Miyagawa-kun and Araya-kun?

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:26.650
I'm amazed you can ask 
such a question so lightly.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:29.310
Y-Yeah? You think so?

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:34.260
I don't think quite as simple
as just saying I love it.

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:35.570
Really?

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:38.850
Well, considering I've been 
playing since I was a kid,

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:40.690
there were times that were rough,

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:42.830
and even times I wanted to quit.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:46.090
To be honest, I can't describe it in a word.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.880
For me, it's not about loving 
it or hating it anymore.

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:53.420
It's sort of like my blood, or my flesh.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:57.090
It's a big part of what makes me who I am.

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:00.640
That's convincing, coming from a 
guy with a body built for tennis!

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:04.670
But at the end of the day, 
since we've all kept it up this long,

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:06.810
we can safely say that we all love it.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.180
I see.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:11.250
<i>That's right.</i>

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:13.870
<i>Tennis brings me joy.</i>

00:18:20.150 --> 00:18:23.990
For the next two months, we're going 
to push your bodies to the limits!

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:32.340
Be careful not to injure yourselves.

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:35.110
Give it all you've got so you'll 
have nothing to regret!

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:43.600
<i>Control!</i>

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:45.400
<i>Yes!</i>

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:46.630
Hey!

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:49.850
Thanks for coming!

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.540
Mom?

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:00.770
We aren't going to train at STC anymore?

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:03.370
There's no reason to go there anymore.

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:04.820
Oh...

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:06.620
Did it inspire you?

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:07.870
Huh?

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:10.830
Yeah...

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:14.120
You'll probably see them all
again at the All-Japan Junior.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:19.730
You're the first seed, Natsu.

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.640
Are you in the opposite block, Akiko?

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:22.170
Yeah.

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:23.450
Bro!

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:25.720
The Kanto Junior match-ups were announced!

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:26.680
What?!

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:32.210
<i>A tournament with sixty-four 
of the best players in Kanto.</i>

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:37.030
<i>Among them, sixteen players will be able 
to participate in the All-Japan Junior.</i>

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:38.570
<i>In other words,</i>

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:42.790
<i>winning twice and making it into the top 
sixteen players is the minimum goal.</i>

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:50.540
Abe Yudai
Yakabe Tadanori
Maruo Eiichiro
Matsuda Takahiro
Ide Yoshiaki

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:46.430
The first seed is Nabae-kun.

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:48.070
Second seed is Okada-kun.

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:50.540
Third seed is our very own Araya-kun.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:53.560
It's pretty much what was expected.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.980
You're up against the fifth-seeded
Ide in your second match,

00:19:56.980 --> 00:19:59.070
which will determine whether 
you go on to the All-Japan.

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:00.700
Ide-kun, as in

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.320
one of the top eight of the 
All-Japan Indoor Invitational?

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.240
It's pretty rigorous, isn't it?

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:10.560
As the runner-up in Kanagawa, 
you're as good as a seeded player.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:15.650
But the Kanto Junior seed order 
is determined by ranking.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:18.100
If you'd won, it would've 
been a different story.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:22.450
Ide dropped down to the top eight 
at the Saitama Junior this year.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:26.710
He's content being a fifth seed, but in 
reality, he's much better than that.

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:29.830
I honestly can't say it's a good match-up,

00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:33.130
but you're aiming to win 
the nationals, after all.

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:34.250
Right.

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:38.340
Like you, I'm also unseeded.

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:41.340
Let's both do our best and 
go to nationals together!

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:44.070
Egawa-kun just keeps getting better.

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:45.840
Yes, he does.

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:47.310
Oh, Takuma!

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:48.350
It's been a while.

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:49.600
Hey.

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:52.600
Look at that entourage of adults.

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:56.440
Takuma-san looks more and more like a pro.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:59.000
Just the other day, he won his second match

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:02.360
and made it into Japan's top ten players.

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:04.160
Top ten?!

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:07.020
He must be here today for 
contracts and press and stuff.

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:09.900
Have a seat right over there.

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:12.680
Um, Takuma-san!

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.840
I know you must be busy,

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:19.380
but sometime soon, can we finish 
our match from last time?

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:24.130
Last time... Oh, that.

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:30.260
<i>The kid went after it on his own...</i>

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:35.270
I won't be in Japan starting next week, so...

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:37.270
It's gotta be today.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:39.990
T-Today?!

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:41.510
Uh, okay!

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:43.320
See you later, then.

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:49.340
You mean the match that Coach Aoi 
called off and made you so frustrated?

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:50.830
Yeah.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:55.410
<i>My mind feels more settled 
after talking to Takuma-san.</i>

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:57.520
<i>If I lose at Kanto</i>

00:21:57.520 --> 00:21:59.650
<i>and lose my chance at nationals,</i>

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:02.210
<i>no companies would want 
to sign me to a contract.</i>

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:08.030
<i>Which means I can't be a player everyone 
places their hopes on, like Takuma-san.</i>

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:11.290
Three-set match.

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:12.970
Egawa to serve!

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:17.210
<i>I thought I might not be able to give 
up on going pro even after losing,</i>

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:20.200
<i>but if I'm not good enough 
to make it to nationals,</i>

00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:23.270
<i>I shouldn't be aiming to go pro.</i>

00:22:27.310 --> 00:22:28.150
<i>But...</i>

00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:31.400
<i>I'll become a pro, no matter what!</i>

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:24.980
Next Time

00:24:00.420 --> 00:24:04.960
The quality of Takuma-san's serve is 
totally different from a few months ago!

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:08.090
It stretches away from my reach after
the bounce, just like Ike-kun's!

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:10.240
Takuma-san is incredible.

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:12.120
It's all I can do just to hold serve!

00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:14.320
Ei-chan's getting better and better!

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:16.050
It's been two years since he started tennis.

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:17.560
Which means... That's right!

00:24:17.560 --> 00:24:20.580
I've known Ei-chan for two years now.

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:22.490
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:24.980
Moonlight and the Sound of Waves

00:24:22.490 --> 00:24:24.130
"Moonlight and the Sound of Waves."

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:31.000
End
